<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tian Yu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> Yu was a Chinese general and frontier official of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a> state during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>. As an officer on the northern frontier he dealt with the Wuhuan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, and he is remembered for setting rival Xianbei chiefs against one another to contain the rising power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kebineng">Kebineng</a>. He later served in campaigns against the state of Wu.</p></div>
